    "summary": "I built a seed-starting tray with four cells, each holding a shallow bin with drain holes. The four full hex bases sit in a tight cluster at (0,0), (1,0), (0,1) and (1,-1). Each one has a third-depth drained bin (hex-bin-third-drain), which is a shallow depth that suits seedlings. Solid end caps close the 14 outer faces and 5 joint bolts lock the bases together. That's 22 parts, with a print estimate of about 1722 g of filament and about 2538 minutes. To show what it's for, each bin is filled with soil and has a seedling in it. The final check passed with no rule issues, the collision check came back clear and there are no prop warnings. The configurator checks fit only, so it can't tell you whether the plastic will cope with water and soil.",
